</surname><given-names>PN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Erythrina studies. Part 7. 2,3-Dihydroauriculatin, a new prenylated isoflavanone from Erythrina senegalensis. Application of the selective INEPT technique</article-title><source>Journal of Natural Products</source><year>1986</year><volume>49</volume><fpage>670</fpage><lpage>673</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3783163</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1021/np50046a019</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Linuma</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Okawa</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanaka</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ho</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kobayashi</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Miyauchi</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Anti-oral microbial activity of isoflavoloids in root bark of Ormosia monosperma</article-title><source>Phytochemistry</source><year>1994</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>889</fpage><lpage>891</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7765696</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0031-9422(00)90378-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wanjala</surname><given-names>CCW</given-names></name><name><surname>Juma</surname><given-names>BF</given-names></name><name><surname>Bojase</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gashe</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Majinda</surname><given-names>RRT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Erythrinaline alkaloids and antimicrobial flavonoids from Erythrina latissima</article-title><source>Planta Medica</source><year>2002</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>640</fpage><lpage>642</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12143000</pu